# Windows / react-native-windows
#
# Regenerated by `npx react-native-windows autolink-windows` (also run
# automatically by `npx react-native run-windows`) every time native
# dependencies change. Committing a stale copy is how this repo ended up
# shipping a build where AutolinkedNativeModules.g.cpp registered zero
# packages -- react-native-fs, react-native-video, etc. were never
# actually linked into the native app, causing the blank-launch crash.
windows/**/AutolinkedNativeModules.g.cpp
windows/**/AutolinkedNativeModules.g.props
windows/**/AutolinkedNativeModules.g.targets
windows/x64/
windows/**/Debug/
windows/**/Release/
windows/**/ARM/
windows/**/ARM64/
windows/**/BundleArtifacts/
windows/**/bin/
windows/**/obj/
windows/**/*.suo
windows/**/*.user
windows/**/*.userosscache
windows/**/*.sln.docstates
windows/**/packages/
windows/**/AppPackages/
windows/**/BundleArtifacts/
windows/**/*.appx
windows/**/*.appxbundle
windows/**/*.appxsym
windows/**/*.msix
windows/**/*.cer
windows/**/*.pfx
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user

